---
description: Full female name in Mali: one given name and one jamu (Aminata Coulibaly, Oumou Sangaré). The surname is drawn from bm.person.lastName, the SAME list a man's is drawn from, because Malian family names carry no gender — compare pl, whose equivalent file must read a separate feminine list. The stronger point for anyone modelling a Malian household is that a woman does NOT take her husband's name at marriage: she keeps her father's jamu for life, so a married couple in one compound have different surnames and their children carry the father's.
generator: tdc
locale: bm
---
<sequence name="p">
  <gen name="f" type="template" value="bm.person.female.firstName"/>
  <gen name="l" type="template" value="bm.person.lastName"/>
</sequence>
<data>${{p.f}} ${{p.l}}</data>
